==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*5 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 30~36.67 seconds<sup>900f~1,100f</sup>.
*2 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 56.67 seconds<sup>1,700f</sup>.
*3 [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 33.33 seconds<sup>1,000f</sup>.
*3 [[Aku Doge]]s spawn after 100 seconds<sup>3,000f</sup>, delay 10~13.33 seconds<sup>300f~400f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Aku Gory|Aku Gories]] spawn after 146.67 seconds<sup>4,400f</sup>, delay 53.33~60 seconds<sup>1,600f~1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]] in this stage are only at 100% magnification, the same strength as in their first appearence in [[Cats of the Cosmos]] chapter 1, so you shouldn't have any problem with them even if you don't have any [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]].

If you have [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Castaway Cat]], [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Neo Psychocat]] and/or [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], they completely destroy the Starred Aliens present, just make sure you properly support them. Otherwise, use strong area attackers such as [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Cyborg Cat]] or [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] to fight off groups of enemies.

The biggest threat here is Aku Gory. Use [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] or [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Maglev Cat]] who not only completely decimate the shields of Aku Doge, but also help mitigate the pushing power of the Starred Aliens. Bring [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] in case you don't destroy the base quick enough and many of the aforementioned Aku Gories start infiltrating your frontlines

